{"entities":[{"text":"Sotalol-induced","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"nifekalant hydrochloride","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"sotalol","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"nifekalant","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"sotalol","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"diltiazem","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"sotalol","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"coronary spasm","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"left ventricular dysfunction","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"VT","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"VT","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"chest discomfort","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"Coronary vasospasm","label":"Disease","id":""}],"entity_aliases":[{"text":"Sotalol","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"sotalol","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"nifekalant","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"nifekalant hydrochloride","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"diltiazem","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"coronary spasm","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"chest discomfort","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"Coronary vasospasm","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","id":"2","label":"Disease"},{"text":"left ventricular dysfunction","id":"2","label":"Disease"},{"text":"VT","id":"3","label":"Disease"},{"text":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","id":"3","label":"Disease"}],"filtered_entities":[{"text":"Sotalol","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"nifekalant hydrochloride","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"diltiazem","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"Coronary vasospasm","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"left ventricular dysfunction","id":"2","label":"Disease"},{"text":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","id":"3","label":"Disease"}],"gold_relations":"sotalol | CID | Coronary vasospasm","labels":"Chemical,Disease","metrics":{"precision":1.0,"recall":1.0,"f1":1.0,"tp":1,"fp":0,"fn":0,"rel_precision":1.0,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":1.0,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":0},"pairs":[{"head":"Sotalol","tail":"Coronary vasospasm","head_id":"1","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"Sotalol","tail":"left ventricular dysfunction","head_id":"1","tail_id":"2"},{"head":"Sotalol","tail":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"1","tail_id":"3"},{"head":"nifekalant hydrochloride","tail":"Coronary vasospasm","head_id":"2","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"nifekalant hydrochloride","tail":"left ventricular dysfunction","head_id":"2","tail_id":"2"},{"head":"nifekalant hydrochloride","tail":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"2","tail_id":"3"},{"head":"diltiazem","tail":"Coronary vasospasm","head_id":"3","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"diltiazem","tail":"left ventricular dysfunction","head_id":"3","tail_id":"2"},{"head":"diltiazem","tail":"sustained ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"3","tail_id":"3"}],"relations":["1 | 1"],"text":"Sotalol-induced coronary spasm in a patient with dilated cardiomyopathy associated with sustained ventricular tachycardia. A 54-year-old man with severe left ventricular dysfunction due to dilated cardiomyopathy was referred to our hospital for symptomatic incessant sustained ventricular tachycardia (VT). After the administration of nifekalant hydrochloride, sustained VT was terminated. An alternate class III agent, sotalol, was also effective for the prevention of VT. However, one month after switching over nifekalant to sotalol, a short duration of ST elevation was documented in ECG monitoring at almost the same time for three consecutive days. ST elevation with chest discomfort disappeared since he began taking long-acting diltiazem. Coronary vasospasm may be induced by the non-selective beta-blocking properties of sotalol."}